---
const faqs = [
  { question: 'I have a tear in my leather seat. Do I need to replace the whole seat?', answer: 'Not at all. In most cases, we can replace just the damaged panel and perfectly match the existing leather or vinyl, saving you significant time and money compared to a full seat replacement.' },
  { question: 'My headliner is sagging. Can you just glue it back up?', answer: 'Unfortunately, gluing a sagging headliner won\'t last because the foam backing underneath has deteriorated. The correct fix—which we specialize in—is to completely remove the old board, strip it clean, and install brand-new foam-backed fabric so it stays up permanently.' },
  { question: 'I\'m restoring a classic car. Can you match the original factory interior?', answer: 'Yes! We love working on classic cars. We have access to huge catalogs of OEM-grade vinyls, leathers, and fabrics. We can rebuild your interior to match its original 1960s or 1970s factory glory, or create a full custom design.' },
  { question: 'How long will my car be in the shop?', answer: 'It depends on the scope of the project. A sagging headliner or a single seat panel repair usually takes just 1 to 2 days. Full custom interior restorations take longer. We always provide a clear timeline before starting any work.' },
  { question: 'Do I need to bring my car in just to get an estimate?', answer: 'While seeing the vehicle in person gives us the most accurate estimate, you can start by sending us clear photos of the damage. We can usually provide a solid ballpark quote right away so you know exactly what to expect.' }
];
---

<section id="faq" class="py-24 px-4 bg-light-bg">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-light-text mb-4">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <p class="text-light-muted">Got questions about your auto upholstery project? We've got answers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6">
      {faqs.map((faq) => (
        <details class="group bg-white p-6 border border-gray-200 shadow-sm cursor-pointer [&_summary::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between font-semibold text-lg text-light-text focus:outline-none">
            {faq.question}
            <span class="transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-180 text-light-accent">
              <svg fill="none" height="24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24"><path d="M6 9l6 6 6-6"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </summary>
          <p class="text-light-muted mt-4 leading-relaxed">
            {faq.answer}
          </p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
